{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>ביראת אלהינו</b> — because of His fear." "<b>תלכו מחרפת הגוים</b> — The meaning: you will not hear their reproach. This was in the sabbatical year, therefore the people cried out. And the count from year twenty to year thirty-two of Darius the Mede is [twelve] years, and from Cyrus [three] years, and forty-four of Ahasuerus — behold forty-four and three years." "<b>ולשון משא</b> — that tied to a bet is like מלוה."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The passage is numerically compressed and possibly corrupt; I have translated hyper-literally. The arithmetic references to regnal years of Darius, Cyrus, and Ahasuerus are rendered exactly as the Hebrew stands, though the count does not straightforwardly resolve."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:15.827950577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}